WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:07.120
Donald Trump dropped an absolutely massive&nbsp;
chaos bomb, just massive dumps of chaos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:13.680
before leaving Washington, D.C. for his Florida&nbsp;
resort yesterday. We already discussed that Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:20.560
vetoed the second coronavirus relief package.&nbsp;
Trump tweeted threats to Iran. And Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:28.080
continues to make completely baseless claims about&nbsp;
supposed voter fraud and now Republicans in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:33.760
House and Senate are apparently trying to figure&nbsp;
out how to deal with what they are increasingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:40.160
describing as an unhinged Trump. And of course,&nbsp;
with all of these stories, we have to understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:46.720
the back story. But we also need to understand&nbsp;
that although it may sound as if these Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:53.600
now accurately are describing what's going on with&nbsp;
Trump, they've been the primary enablers of Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.560 --> 00:01:01.040
for a very long time. And Trump has been unhinged&nbsp;
and continues being unhinged. So the Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:06.080
now saying, whoa, Trump's acting a little&nbsp;
bit crazy. They deserve none of our sympathy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:10.480
and they deserve much of the blame. Now, I already&nbsp;
told you in the earlier segment that Donald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:15.440
Trump's behavior with regard to trying to overturn&nbsp;
the election has put him at odds with his own vice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:20.720
president, Mike Pence, his own secretary of state,&nbsp;
his own White House counsel and many other people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:26.080
Now, we're hearing from many sources that&nbsp;
aides around Donald Trump at the White House&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:32.800
are increasingly disturbed by his anti-democratic&nbsp;
behavior. But since Trump posted that absurd video&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:38.960
screed on Tuesday making all sorts of false claims&nbsp;
about the stimulus package and after he dropped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:45.040
that chaos bomb yesterday before leaving, we're&nbsp;
hearing from more and more Republicans and aides&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:51.120
to Republicans that there is genuine concern about&nbsp;
what Trump is doing here. One Republican aide said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:58.160
to CNN that Trump is, quote, coming unhinged. Now,&nbsp;
he's been unhinged for years. House Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:04.880
actually had a phone call yesterday to talk about&nbsp;
what to do about Donald Trump's bizarre threats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:10.080
and his reaction to the stimulus package, which,&nbsp;
of course, ended up with a veto. As we already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:16.160
discussed. Republican Congressman Don Bacon&nbsp;
says Trump has thrown Republicans under the bus.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:23.280
And there are apparently also concerns that some&nbsp;
Republicans will bow to Trump's pressure to try&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:30.160
to challenge the counting of the electoral vote&nbsp;
on January 6th. Now, to be clear, nobody thinks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:36.880
that they would have enough support to actually&nbsp;
make a difference and overturn the results. Mitch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:42.480
McConnell has been telling Senate Republicans&nbsp;
do not get involved in this effort to challenge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:48.640
the results on January 6th. But there's concern&nbsp;
about how to handle the optics if some Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:55.120
did bow to Donald Trump's pressure. So let's talk&nbsp;
a little bit more about that. There is no way that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.120 --> 00:03:00.560
Republicans are going to change the outcome of&nbsp;
the Electoral College vote going for Joe Biden.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:07.840
But it is conceivable that Trump will get some&nbsp;
House Republicans to object to the count for Joe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:15.680
Biden to get electoral votes from six states that&nbsp;
Biden won. And if House Republicans and Trump can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:21.440
convince just a single Republican senator to&nbsp;
join them in their objections, theoretically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:27.680
they could force a vote in both chambers, which&nbsp;
Republicans and Democrats still believe would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:32.000
lead to Joe Biden winning. But again, it would&nbsp;
look disastrous for Republicans in a number of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:38.560
different ways. Those who might vote to give Trump&nbsp;
the presidency if such a vote were forced would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:44.400
completely humiliate, humiliated nationally. And&nbsp;
those who vote that Biden should be president.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:50.320
Republicans might suffer the wrath of Trump&nbsp;
in their constituencies. Now, increasingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:55.600
I'm getting the sense that even though these&nbsp;
very Republicans are the people responsible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.600 --> 00:04:00.640
for what Donald Trump did over the last four&nbsp;
years, they likely are setting themselves up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:06.800
at least many of them, to sort of pretend they&nbsp;
were never really on Trump's side, even to pretend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:12.720
Trump sort of didn't happen after Donald Trump&nbsp;
leaves office and to very quickly move on and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:20.240
get back to partizan business as usual. We care&nbsp;
about the debt. We we have to stop socialism.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:25.760
We have to stop government takeovers of this, that&nbsp;
and the other things. But before that happens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:33.840
prepare yourselves for a very, very wacky few&nbsp;
weeks. And we'll have more coverage of this on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:40.320
show's Instagram at David Pakman show. And make&nbsp;
sure you're following me on Instagram as well at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:46.480
David Pakman. And we'll take a quick break. And we&nbsp;
will be speaking to Mark Tushnet after the break.&nbsp;

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:52.000
Do we really need the Supreme Court? A very&nbsp;
interesting perspective from Mark Tushnet.

